This project is licensed in three parts, because it contains three kinds of
thing.  Read the part that covers the file you are interested in.

  1. The game — code, writing, characters, design.  © 2026 Grant van Zyl,
     licensed CC BY-NC-ND 4.0.  Everything except the files listed in parts 2
     and 3.

  2. The character sprite art and the world atlas.  Third-party pixel art by
     the Liberated Pixel Cup community, licensed OGA-BY 3.0 (some contributions
     CC0).  NOT covered by part 1 — see below.

  3. The sanitary sheet, art/sprites/sanitary.png.  Third-party pixel art by
     Matthew Nash, licensed CC-BY-SA 3.0.  ShareAlike, so it carries an
     obligation parts 1 and 2 do not, and it is in a file of its own for
     exactly that reason — see below.

The split is deliberate.  Part 1's NoDerivatives term is ours to place on our
own work; it is not ours to place on somebody else's art, and doing so would
misrepresent the terms that art actually carries.  Parts 2 and 3 are separate
from each other for the mirror-image reason: part 3's ShareAlike term is not
ours to place on part 2's artists' work, and packing the two into one sheet
would do precisely that.


